 ],
 "notes": "Where the list is: it starts at the foot of p. 63 (n70.jpg) and runs onto the top of p. 64 (n71.jpg). n68, n69 and n72 don't contain it. Both pages carry the column headings '79 '80 '81 '82 '83 above the asterisks. No sentence explains the asterisks. They are almost certainly the years each station sent returns, because the '83 column holds 17 stations if the braced pair 93/94 counts once, and the text above says \"We have received filled schedules from seventeen stations.\" The list numbers 34 stations (81–115, with no. 106 missing), which matches \"Schedules were sent to thirty-four stations\". The empty nos. 116, 117, 118, \"119 [1880]\" and 120 come after 115 and are left out, as you asked.\n\nHow the asterisks were read: in the marks field I give the year columns I take each asterisk to sit under. The print uses two kinds of asterisk (bold and light), which sit at slightly different positions. So on p. 64 a row's year columns come from where its asterisks start and how far apart they are. The rows that start at the '79 column are 92, 99, 100, 104, 111 and 114. Rows 91, 98, 101 and 110 start at '80. In printed I give the asterisks without the empty columns.\n\nThings printed in the list:\n- Ditto marks: \",,\" after a height means \"ft.\", taken from the first row. As a place, \",,\" stands for the place above it: Sutherland for 82 (Rhu Stoir), Wigtonshire for 112–114. I kept \",,\" in place, as printed.\n- 114 and 115 have no \",,\" after their heights (325 and 175).\n- 93 and 94: Hynish Signal Tower, Tyree, and Skerryvore, off Tyree, are joined by a brace. They share one row of asterisks, one height (150) and one keeper (Wm. Crow). I gave them two entries carrying the same shared fields. Hynish was Skerryvore's shore station.\n- 86 Monach Isles: two heights (150 and 62) are stacked in a brace, and a second brace joins them to \"J.Youngclause\". The General Remarks below the list call him \"Mr. James Youngclause, Monach lighthouse\". The same remarks give Barra Head's keeper as \"Mr. William Irvine\".\n- 92: a vertical bar is printed between \"Ardnamurchan Pt.\" and \"Argyl.\" I put the bar in printed and left it out of the name and place fields.\n- Spacing: the type is set tight in \"J.Youngclause\", \"Robt.Laidlaw\" and \"Alex.Murray\". I copied \"J.Youngclause\" as printed but normalised the other two to \"Robt. Laidlaw\" and \"Alex. Murray\". Adjust them if you want that spacing kept exactly.\n- Type and character: no row gives a type (L.H./L.V.) or a description of the light, so those fields are null throughout.\n\nSpellings as printed (not corrected):\n- Kircudbright (for Kirkcudbright)\n- Rosshire (for Ross-shire)\n- Argyl. (an abbreviation)\n- Wigtonshire (the usual spelling at the time)\n- Dhuheartach (Dubh Artach)\n- Rhuvaal (Rubh' a' Mhàil)\n- Lochindaul (Loch Indaal)\n- Island Glass (Eilean Glas)\n- Rhu Stoir (Stoer Head)\n- Devaar (Davaar)\n- Tyree (Tiree)\n\nOCR errors corrected from the scans: the OCR has Kyleakin's height as 58, but the scan reads 53. It also misreads \"Loch Eil\" as \"Loch Hil\", \"Rhinns of Islay\" as \"Bhinne of Iglavs\", Mull of Kintyre's 297 as \"7\", Pladda's 130 as \"Teo\", and Mull of Galloway's 325 as \"3825\".",
